; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Times Tables on a Circle
; CATEGORY: Mathematics
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     multiplication, modular arithmetic, circles, patterns, cardioid
; SUMMARY:  Places 120 points on a circle and joins each point n to point m times n, revealing hearts and flowers.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Number 120 points around a circle from 0 to 119. For the 2 times
;   table, join point 1 to point 2, point 2 to point 4, point 3 to
;   point 6 and so on. When the answer is bigger than 119, wrap round
;   the circle (that is, take the remainder after dividing by 120).
;   The straight lines add up to a curve: the 2 times table makes a
;   heart shape called a cardioid. Six tables are drawn side by side.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the list "tables to try other multipliers,
;   and :points to use more or fewer points.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * MODULO to wrap numbers around a circle, like hours on a clock
;   * finding the point at a given angle with SIN and COS
;   * how many straight lines can draw a curve (an envelope)
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Is the 61 times table with 120 points the same as the 1 times
;     table? What about 121?
;   * Try the 2 times table with 12 points, then 300 points.
;   * Use decimals like 2.5: change MODULO to work with the
;     fractional point positions.
; ============================================================

make "points 120
make "tables [2 3 4 5 8 51]
make "radius 115
make "colors [[220 60 80] [240 140 30] [50 160 90] [40 120 210] [130 80 200] [200 70 170]]

; Where point k sits on a circle centered at (cx, cy).
; Point 0 is at the left, like the 9 on a clock face.
to spot :k :cx :cy
  localmake "angle 270 + 360 * :k / :points
  output list :cx + :radius * sin :angle :cy + :radius * cos :angle
end

to circletable :m :cx :cy :color
  ; the circle itself
  setpencolor [200 200 200] setpensize 1
  penup setxy :cx :cy pendown arc 360 :radius penup
  ; one chord from every point k to point m*k (wrapped round)
  setpencolor :color
  for [k 1 :points - 1] [
    penup setpos spot :k :cx :cy
    pendown setpos spot modulo :m * :k :points :cx :cy
  ]
  penup setxy :cx - 30 :cy - :radius - 22 setpencolor [60 60 60] setlabelheight 15
  label word :m "| times|
end

clearscreen hideturtle
foreach :tables [
  localmake "col remainder (# - 1) 3
  localmake "row int ((# - 1) / 3)
  circletable ? -260 + 260 * :col 140 - 290 * :row item # :colors
]
